1
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:57,900
Oh, it's a quarter to four,

2
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:00,400
and I have a production meeting at four.

3
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:02,900
I planned to take you for a ride in Central Park

4
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,600
in a horse and carriage.

5
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:06,000
Harry, I'd love to,

6
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,300
but I have work to do.

7
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:12,035
OK. We'll walk back to your office with you.

8
00:01:12,035 --> 00:01:14,135
It's so nice out.

9
00:01:14,135 --> 00:01:17,000
I decided to forget about my accounting problems

10
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,400
and just enjoy this beautiful spring day.

11
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,800
Take the time, Susan.

12
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:23,400
I know I should,

13
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:27,600
but ... well, there are too many things to do.

14
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:29,000
I understand.

15
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,700
I'll go for a ride with Michelle.

16
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,870
Right.

17
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:37,100
Well, I had a really nice time.

18
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:38,452
So did I.

19
00:01:38,452 --> 00:01:39,600
So did I.

20
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:42,700
I'm sorry you can't come with us, Susan.

21
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:44,200
So am I.

22
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,079
Bye-bye.

23
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:55,200
Harry! Michelle! Can you wait till I make a phone call?

24
00:01:55,200 --> 00:02:10,282
Sure.

25
00:02:10,282 --> 00:02:12,243
Susan Stewart's office.

26
00:02:12,243 --> 00:02:13,705
Sam, this is Susan.

27
00:02:13,705 --> 00:02:15,068
Hi. How was lunch?

28
00:02:15,068 --> 00:02:16,800
Fine.

29
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:18,193
You're late.

30
00:02:18,193 --> 00:02:20,810
The production department's waiting in the conference room.

31
00:02:20,810 --> 00:02:21,675
I know.

32
00:02:21,675 --> 00:02:23,486
Ask Paul Smith to fill in for me.

33
00:02:23,486 --> 00:02:24,939
He knows everything about the production schedule,

34
00:02:24,939 --> 00:02:27,018
and he can answer any questions.

35
00:02:27,018 --> 00:02:28,262
Right.

36
00:02:28,262 --> 00:02:29,556
Don't tell any one,

37
00:02:29,556 --> 00:02:32,700
but I'm taking a little time to smell the flowers.

38
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:32,900
Good for you.

39
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,700
It'll be our secret.

40
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:36,300
But schedule another production meeting for tomorrow.

41
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,700
I'll be back

42
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:38,700
for my six o'clock appointment with Mr. Ozawa.

43
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:39,725
OK, Susan.

44
00:02:39,725 --> 00:02:41,100
And have a nice afternoon.

45
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:48,902
Thanks.

46
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:48,902
She likes you.

47
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:48,902
I know. I like her.

48
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:48,902
How'd you do it?

49
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:48,902
We had a talk.

50
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:48,902
About what?

51
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:48,902
Life.

52
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:48,902
And what did you decide?

53
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:48,902
That's a secret ... between us women.
